    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\">2017-03-28 13:59 GMT+02:00 MJH <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">harv...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span>:<br></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello, <div><br></div><div>I am new to using simmer for DES (coming from the world of Simul8). This is a great tool and thanks for all the hard work you&#39;ve put in. I normally use these programs for healthcare simulation and have a question about simulating different patient arrival times throughout the day. </div><div><br></div><div>Is there currently a way to run a simulation for (as an example) 5 days, where patients would arrive at different rates between 3 different periods in the day. Such as</div><div><br></div><div>1 patient every 10 mins from 8am to 4pm</div><div>1 patient every 30 mins from 4pm to 12am</div><div>1 patient every 60 mins from 12am to 8am</div><div><br></div><div>I got the general idea to work fine using the code below (defining different patient types, though if there is a simpler way to do this, then I&#39;m happy to take on suggestions), but then if I wanted to simulate this over 5 days, is there a way to reset the clock at minute 1440 (midnight) on day one, so that I don&#39;t need to define 15 different groups of patients?  </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div>simmer() %&gt;%<br></div><div>    </div><div>    ...</div><div><br></div><div>    add_generator(&quot;patient_on_&quot;, patient_traj, from_to(0, 8*24, function() rexp(1, rate = 1/60), arrive = F), mon = 2) %&gt;% <br></div><div><div>    add_generator(&quot;patient_am_&quot;, patient_traj, from_to(8*24, 16*60, function() rexp(1, rate = 1/15), arrive = F), mon = 2) %&gt;% <br></div></div><div><div>    add_generator(&quot;patient_pm_&quot;, patient_traj, from_to(16*60, 24*60, function() rexp(1, rate = 1/15), arrive = F), mon = 2) %&gt;% <br></div></div><div>  <br></div><div>    run(60*24*5)</div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><br></div></font></span></div></div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
